{"sessionId":"3f83e8","location":"global:input","message":"rich-editable-input","data":{"inputType":"insertFromPaste","data":null,"domText":"DEBUG MODE.\n\nThe handwriting coordinate bug is NOT fixed.\n\nC"},"hypothesisId":"C","runId":"post-fix","timestamp":1781098895470}
{"sessionId":"3f83e8","location":"RichEditableLine:onInput","message":"onInput-commit","data":{"id":"nb-25","plain":"DEBUG MODE.\n\nThe handwriting coordinate bug is NOT fixed.\n\nCurrent behavior:\nWhen I draw in the handwriting canvas, the ink appears noticeably lower than the cursor/stylus position. Screenshot confirms vertical offset.\n\nThis is a blocking bug before iPad testing.\n\nDo NOT add features.\nDo NOT refactor.\nDo NOT change architecture.\nDo NOT touch Math Zone.\nDo NOT touch FreeformCanvas unless a real proven cause requires it.\n\nFix only the Canvas coordinate mapping in HandwritingBlock.\n\nImportant:\nThe rendered stroke must appear exactly under the pointer.\n\nInvestigate and fix:\n\n1. Make sure pointer coordinates are calculated from the actual canvas element:\n   const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect()\n   x = (event.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width\n   y = (event.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height\n\n2. Make sure no toolbar/header/padding height is included in the drawing coordinate calculation.\n\n3. Make sure canvas internal bitmap size and CSS visual size match:\n   - CSS size comes from getBoundingClientRect()\n   - internal canvas.width = rect.width * devicePixelRatio\n   - internal canvas.height = rect.height * devicePixelRatio\n   - ctx.setTransform(devicePixelRatio, 0, 0, devicePixelRatio, 0, 0)\n   - draw using CSS pixel coordinates, not mixed DPR coordinates\n\n4. Check whether any parent element uses transform/scale.\n   If yes, getBoundingClientRect() should still be the source of truth.\n\n5. Add temporary debug logging only if needed:\n   - clientX/clientY\n   - rect.left/top/width/height\n   - normalized x/y\n   - canvas.width/height\n   - devicePixelRatio\n   Remove or gate logs after fixing.\n\n6. Verify with three tests:\n   - draw at top-left of canvas\n   - draw at center\n   - draw at bottom-right\n   The ink should appear exactly under the cursor in all three.\n\n7. Run build/typecheck.\n\nReport:\n- root cause\n- exact files changed\n- what coordinate math changed\n- verification result\n\nDo not mark fixed until the cursor and ink align visually.","suppressed":false,"programmatic":false,"toolbarGuard":false,"ignoreBlock":false},"hypothesisId":"D","runId":"pre-fix","timestamp":1781098895472}
{"sessionId":"3f83e8","location":"ProjectNotebookBlock:updateBlockText","message":"update-block-text","data":{"id":"nb-25","rawText":"DEBUG MODE.\n\nThe handwriting coordinate bug is NOT fixed.\n\nCurrent behavior:\nWhen I draw in the handwriting canvas, the ink appears noticeably lower than the cursor/stylus position. Screenshot confirms vertical offset.\n\nThis is a blocking bug before iPad testing.\n\nDo NOT add features.\nDo NOT refactor.\nDo NOT change architecture.\nDo NOT touch Math Zone.\nDo NOT touch FreeformCanvas unless a real proven cause requires it.\n\nFix only the Canvas coordinate mapping in HandwritingBlock.\n\nImportant:\nThe rendered stroke must appear exactly under the pointer.\n\nInvestigate and fix:\n\n1. Make sure pointer coordinates are calculated from the actual canvas element:\n   const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect()\n   x = (event.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width\n   y = (event.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height\n\n2. Make sure no toolbar/header/padding height is included in the drawing coordinate calculation.\n\n3. Make sure canvas internal bitmap size and CSS visual size match:\n   - CSS size comes from getBoundingClientRect()\n   - internal canvas.width = rect.width * devicePixelRatio\n   - internal canvas.height = rect.height * devicePixelRatio\n   - ctx.setTransform(devicePixelRatio, 0, 0, devicePixelRatio, 0, 0)\n   - draw using CSS pixel coordinates, not mixed DPR coordinates\n\n4. Check whether any parent element uses transform/scale.\n   If yes, getBoundingClientRect() should still be the source of truth.\n\n5. Add temporary debug logging only if needed:\n   - clientX/clientY\n   - rect.left/top/width/height\n   - normalized x/y\n   - canvas.width/height\n   - devicePixelRatio\n   Remove or gate logs after fixing.\n\n6. Verify with three tests:\n   - draw at top-left of canvas\n   - draw at center\n   - draw at bottom-right\n   The ink should appear exactly under the cursor in all three.\n\n7. Run build/typecheck.\n\nReport:\n- root cause\n- exact files changed\n- what coordinate math changed\n- verification result\n\nDo not mark fixed until the cursor and ink align visually.","marksOverrideLen":0},"hypothesisId":"D","runId":"pre-fix","timestamp":1781098895472}
